or public repository access should be interpreted as an automatic grant of trademark rights.

Trademark permissions must be separately established where required.

---

## 21. Reservation of Rights

All rights relating to project names, marks, logos and associated branding are reserved to the extent provided by applicable law.

Nothing in this policy transfers ownership of project identifiers.

---

## 22. Enforcement

The project may take appropriate action under applicable law against uses of project names or branding that:

* intentionally create confusion;
* falsely imply endorsement;
* falsely imply certification;
* impersonate official project channels;
* misrepresent third-party implementations as official;
* misuse project branding in a materially misleading manner.

Nothing in this section requires enforcement against accurate descriptive or legally protected uses.

---

## 23. Independent Research Freedom

This trademark policy is not intended to restrict legitimate scientific criticism or independent research.

Researchers remain free to:

* study GNOSIS;
* test GNOSIS;
* criticize GNOSIS;
* compare GNOSIS with competing architectures;
* publish negative results;
* publish positive results;
* develop independent implementations;

subject to the applicable software license and applicable law.

Scientific criticism does not constitute trademark misuse merely because it identifies the project by name.

---

